1
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:12,960
Brighten it up,
then step back and take a look.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,660
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out to you.

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:35,340
Walking while looking back,
hand in hand with Mom.

4
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:42,440
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:53,520
So I tried walking on only the
black tiles of the arcade street.

6
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:01,800
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

7
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,140
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-shadowed aunties who are a thorn in your side too.

8
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,700
Come on, turn that corner over there.

9
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,920
You can meet everyone, everyone!

10
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,840
Over there is Kame surely there's Kame.

11
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town.

12
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

13
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,620
Memories of Shinobazu Pond.

14
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:45,280
That was wonderful, wasn't it.

15
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,900
You can really feel the European tradition.

16
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,160
To me, they all just looked the same.

17
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:55,560
Ryo-chan was looking forward to
eating together on the way home.

18
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:56,980
That's why he tagged along, isn't it.

19
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,400
So, what should we get? Eel or sushi?

20
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,000
How about the zoo? That'd be nice too.

21
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,720
Yeah, that's right.

22
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:07,840
It's a bit too early to eat, though.

23
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:11,520
Hey, the weather's nice.
Shall we all go out on a boat?

24
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:12,860
Sounds good, let's go.

25
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,080
Is there a place to ride boats in Ueno?

26
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,980
Shinobazu Pond.

27
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:19,440
It's right after you come down the hill.

28
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,200
Look, it's over there.

29
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,660
Let's see, then.

30
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,100
Alright, I've decided on that one.

31
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:39,400
Pedal boat sounds fun, so that's the one.

32
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:42,400
Shall we go with this one?

33
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,500
Yeah, let's go with this one.

34
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,320
Nana-chan, want to give rowing a try?

35
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,160
It's been ages since I've been on a boat.

36
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:57,100
Hey, wait! What's so fun about
riding a pedal boat all by myself?

37
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:59,000
But you said you'd...

38
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Yes, I did.

39
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,240
I decide. Honda's riding with me.

40
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,780
Princess Foto, you ride with Reiko.

41
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,740
And Nakagawa, you ride alone.

42
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,680
Why am I the only one riding alone?

43
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,140
This boat seats three, so -

44
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,180
just ride with Reiko-san and the others.

45
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,640
Anyway, I'm getting in.

46
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:19,500
Yes.

47
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:23,020
Since we're here,
I really wanted to ride with Nana-chan.

48
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,020
But I've decided on a spot further in.

49
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:27,900
Why do we have to ride with each other?
Cut me some slack.

50
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,900
This is the most stylish way to do it.

51
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:33,420
Ryo-chan, you really wanted to
ride with Honda-san, didn't you?

52
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:34,680
No, it's fine.

53
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,060
There sure are a lot of birds, Senpai.

54
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:45,120
Those are seagulls.
They've been multiplying lately, too.

55
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,560
Look, the ducks are following us.

56
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,740
They're so cute.

57
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:56,260
Right, I'll try giving them some biscuits.

58
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,860
Nana-chan is feeding the ducks.

59
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,340
She's so kind.

60
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,820
What? Oh no.

61
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:12,580
Hey, you can't feed them!

62
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:23,840
No.

63
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,100
No, this is bad.

64
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,680
Who was it? I told them.

65
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,040
Mama-chan!

66
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:37,980
If you're holding food, they'll all swarm you!
Throw the food away quickly!

67
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:38,440
Yes!

68
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,960
Catch you! Ponta-san!

69
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,280
Stop it!

70
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,980
Don't!

71
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,040
I was scared.

72
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:05,360
And with Tsuchisaku-san mixed in,
the pigeons and crows came too!

73
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:06,860
Are you alright?

74
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:10,820
Seagulls are pretty, though.
I was surprised.

75
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,160
How about we race?

76
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,100
Whoever reaches the other
side of the pond first wins.

77
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:19,300
The loser treats for today's meal.

78
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,060
Reiko-san is at a disadvantage.

79
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,060
Let's go.

80
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,440
Ready, set, go!

81
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,080
What should we do?

82
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:32,920
I hate seeing that smug face.
Let's take the challenge, Kei-chan.

83
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,743
Okay, damn it.

84
00:05:40,793 --> 00:05:43,660
That boat's inefficient.
We're at a disadvantage.

85
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,680
They're catching up to Center!

86
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,840
Dammit! Pick up the pace!

87
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,940
I can't go any faster!

88
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,960
Sorry, senpai, going ahead.

89
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,920
Ryo-chan, you're buying lunch, right?

90
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:08,180
Aaaaah! Today, to win, not being
picky about the means is our strength!

91
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,260
Aaaaah!

92
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:14,040
Me? Nooo!

93
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:20,640
Honda, I'm counting on you with the steering!
Kanakana!

94
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:22,540
Aaaaah!

95
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:27,760
Nngh! Don't you dare go dying on me!

96
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,720
Let's do it!

97
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,300
It's not fun at all!

98
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,240
This is the natural way, you know.

99
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,040
That's right.

100
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:09,320
Damn it!

101
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:11,960
Shut up!

102
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,060
What's wrong?

103
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,100
Water's coming up from under the pond...

104
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,400
It's spurting out!

105
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:24,000
They're circulating the
pond water with a pump.

106
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,860
Why's that?

107
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:28,180
Because sludge used to build
up there and made it filthy.

108
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:32,180
They create a current with the pump
to purify the water artificially.

109
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:33,920
I see.

110
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,287
Senpai,

111
00:07:35,337 --> 00:07:38,740
there's a weird fish floating up here!

112
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:39,680
Let's see.

113
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,640
Look.

114
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:46,580
That's not a fish.
It's a model of a submarine or something.

115
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:47,720
A toy?

116
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,740
Someone must have been playing with it and

117
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:52,280
W-wait, this is...

118
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,520
What's wrong?

119
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,320
And it's from our
elementary school days, too.

120
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,360
No way.

121
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,920
No, look, the name is carved right into it.

122
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,320
It really is.

123
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:04,540
But why is it showing up now?

124
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:08,340
The lead weight came loose, and the water
circulation brought it up to the surface.

125
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:12,520
Did you two sail boats in this pond
when you were in elementary school?

126
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,380
Yeah, I came here every day.

127
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,820
Back in elementary school,
submarines were a huge craze.

128
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,580
I bought and built almost
every model kit there was.

129
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:24,020
First you get the propeller
going and make it run.

130
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:28,280
But in a bathtub you can see it sink too clearly,
so it's not much fun.

131
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:32,380
Rice paddies and ponds are more realistic,
since it vanishes from sight underwater.

132
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,340
It looks really cool.

133
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:38,480
But after they sink,
so many never float back up.

134
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:42,320
Some get tangled in
the weeds and can't move.

135
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:46,240
The dive angle is too steep,
so they stick into the bottom of the pond.

136
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:49,340
The weights are too heavy,
and there are all sorts of other causes.

137
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:54,680
We often held submarine
contests in this Shinobazu Pond.

138
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:57,140
I'd guess about 100 of them
have sunk to the bottom.

139
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,660
A hundred?

140
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:01,680
I've got it.

141
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,900
I've had a brilliant idea.

142
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:05,820
Where are you going?

143
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,420
What's that?

144
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:10,500
It's a dip net.

145
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,760
I borrowed it from the folk museum.

146
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,980
Let's survey the bottom
of the pond with this.

147
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:18,000
I wonder if you can
catch anything with that.

148
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,500
I'm a dip-net genius. Leave it to me.

149
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:23,320
Okay, like this...

150
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,680
Look, we've got a huge haul!

151
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,560
Wow.

152
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:32,700
This is...

153
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:38,360
It's the GI Castle and
underwater scooter I lost.

154
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,980
Is that one yours too?

155
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,180
There might be more stuff down there.

156
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,680
It's like a treasure hunt, isn't it?

157
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:48,940
It's heavy.

158
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:49,680
What is it?

159
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:49,820
What?

160
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:59,280
This is the anatomy model I sank here.

161
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,080
Why would something
like that be in the pond?

162
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,900
I took it from the elementary school
science room to scare everyone,

163
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:10,940
set it up here,
and then I completely forgot about it.

164
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:13,120
Shocked?

165
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,800
So it finally surfaced.

166
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:22,000
It's clogged up with rice and sesame.

167
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,100
Those are my short pants.

168
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,640
Why are they in the pond?

169
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,180
When even things like
this start turning up...

170
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:32,580
This is...

171
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:36,860
Takayama

172
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,000
Takayama

173
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:45,680
Takayama

174
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,140
Hey, Takayama, hurry up!

175
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,020
Alright, I'm going first!

176
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,780
Alright, me too.

177
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,543
Hey,

178
00:11:00,593 --> 00:11:04,900
What's wrong, Takayama?

179
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,440
It's not scary, just jump!

180
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,800
What's wrong, what's wrong?

181
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,080
Jump, jump, Takayama!

182
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,846
Hmm hmm hmm hmm

183
00:11:12,896 --> 00:11:15,712
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

184
00:11:15,762 --> 00:11:18,553
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

185
00:11:18,603 --> 00:11:21,760
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

186
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:24,588
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

187
00:11:24,638 --> 00:11:27,467
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

188
00:11:27,517 --> 00:11:30,320
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...

189
00:11:30,370 --> 00:11:33,620
Ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh...
ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... ugh... u...

190
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,820
Oh no, I had 100 rice-and-sesame
snacks in my pocket!

191
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,320
It's not coming back up!

192
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:49,980
I was trying to scare you, that's all!

193
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:53,560
This is bad!

194
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:54,400
Kankichi!

195
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:59,940
Kankichi, are you okay?

196
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,280
That was close.

197
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:01,320
Here it comes!

198
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,420
Heave-ho!

199
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:13,100
My pants and underwear came off together!

200
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:40,060
Just as expected of Kankichi!

201
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:42,500
He's good at getting people
to do this kind of thing.

202
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:54,840
Takayama, did you hit your finger again?

203
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,200
Just a little mistake.

204
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,120
Bro.

205
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,820
Did you forget your umbrella?

206
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:33,740
Bro, your finger.

207
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:35,680
It's nothing.

208
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,900
This time I'm definitely taking first place.

209
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,860
Hey, Takayama.

210
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,640
No, you've had me laughing today.

211
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:52,720
Nobody else could copy hitting all
five fingers with a hammer, right?

212
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,840
Hahahaha.

213
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,240
Jiro

214
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,000
Alright, come at me!

215
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,700
That hurts! Cut it out!

216
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,560
Wow.

217
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:25,780
My big brother, you know,

218
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:28,860
got picked for the relay team
at the sports day the other day!

219
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:32,120
Both of my big brothers
are class representatives!

220
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,320
My big brother's a
first-degree black belt in judo!

221
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:35,960
Wow, that's amazing.

222
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:39,160
Well, we don't have anything
to brag about here, do we?

223
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,680
What about Jiron's big brother?

224
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:44,230
My big brother is...

225
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,700
My big brother is...

226
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:49,920
He's great at pro-level model building!

227
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:55,460
He's really good, you know!
Airplanes, submarines, you name it!

228
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:59,420
So you're entering the
submarine contest on Sunday?

229
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,240
W-well, yeah...

230
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:04,840
I'm definitely going to watch!

231
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:05,440
Me too!

232
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:09,280
Hey!

233
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,800
Kankichi, get back here!

234
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,120
Hey!

235
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:15,500
Hey! Stop right there!

236
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,260
Kankichi.

237
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,800
Didn't Takayama Kankichi
come running this way?

238
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:27,740
Out the window, outside.

239
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:28,480
I see.

240
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:32,480
That Kankichi! When I see him on Monday,
I'm going to give him a good scolding.

241
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:37,400
The teacher's gone, Kankichi-kun.

242
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:46,760
Are you okay?

243
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:49,940
Ow that was a lifesaver.

244
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:53,480
But the teacher said he'll
really give it to us on Monday.

245
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:56,120
He'll have forgotten all about it by Monday.

246
00:15:57,242 --> 00:16:02,480
Takayama, you actually make model kits too?

247
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,480
Still, you're really bad at it.

248
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:07,200
With gaps like these, it won't float up.

249
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:10,760
So it's no good after all

250
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,470
Oh, I see.

251
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,960
It's for my little brother.

252
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:19,360
I kept it a secret because
I wanted to surprise him.

253
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:23,560
I'm bad at sports,
and my grades are just average.

254
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:27,860
On top of that, I'm clumsy, so I've
never really acted like a big brother.

255
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,180
So that's why you stayed
behind to work on it.

256
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,320
Yeah, but it just isn't turning out right.

257
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:38,220
Alright, then I'll help you out.

258
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:43,880
I've got a younger brother named Kinjirō too,
so I know exactly how you feel.

259
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,440
But unlike me, Kankitsu-kun...

260
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:50,740
No, Kinjirō's the good student,
unlike me, right?

261
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:54,620
I'm not exactly the kind of big brother
my little brother can brag about, either.

262
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,520
Kankitsu-kun.

263
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:59,820
I'll help, but you're the one
who has to build it, got it?

264
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:00,320
Yeah.

265
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:05,160
First, file off the burrs well, then fit
the parts together once before you glue them.

266
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:05,720
Yeah.

267
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,960
Go easy on the glue.

268
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:15,180
Big brother, are you entering
tomorrow's submarine contest?

269
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:18,760
Yeah, I don't know if I'll win, though.

270
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:21,100
Hey, have you already made the submarine?

271
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,360
I'm in the middle of making it right now.

272
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,660
Show me, show me!

273
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:28,700
The glue hasn't dried yet,
so if you touch it, it'll break.

274
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:31,100
You'll have to wait until the contest.

275
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:35,700
I didn't know you were really good at pro-level model making,
big brother.

276
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,780
Y-yes! Yay!

277
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:48,880
The contest starts in the afternoon,
so we'll do a test run before that.

278
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:49,560
Yeah.

279
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,480
Do you think it'll work?

280
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:59,000
Don't worry.
Even I can see this one's well made.

281
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:02,960
Is that so?
If Kankichi-kun says so, I feel relieved.

282
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:06,320
Here goes.

283
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,160
Go!

284
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:12,500
Whoa...

285
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:17,820
It sank.

286
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,040
Yay!

287
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:26,900
Nice!

288
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:28,900
Amazing, amazing!

289
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,260
We did it, Kankichi-kun!

290
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:37,010
Thanks.
It's all thanks to you, Kankichi-kun.

291
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:39,400
With this,
I can proudly brag to my little brother.

292
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:41,478
Nah. Anyway, Takayama,

293
00:18:41,528 --> 00:18:44,520
let's try moving it more toward the middle.

294
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:47,240
But what if we can't get it back?

295
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:48,720
It'll be fine.

296
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,120
It's going great!

297
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:13,920
What's this?

298
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:15,640
What's going on? What's going on?

299
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:18,780
Kankichi-kun, let's get it back from him.

300
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:20,100
It's just a brat's toy, you know.

301
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,200
Sorry.

302
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,640
Please give back that submarine.

303
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:25,860
What did you say?

304
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:29,340
You wake me up from a good nap,
and now you want it back?

305
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:32,420
What's with that face?

306
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,020
Got a problem with that?

307
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:39,120
No problem, I just want it back, okay?

308
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:42,820
No way.

309
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:47,040
Perfect, let's play with this to kill time.

310
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,240
Now that's a good idea.

311
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:51,420
Let's hit it with a rock
while it's moving and sink it.

312
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:54,240
After all that work we put into it!

313
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,060
I said give it back, give it back!

314
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:58,120
What did you say?

315
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,840
What a cheeky brat.

316
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:02,200
If you want it back, come and get it.

317
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,660
Kankichi, what should we do?

318
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:08,340
Hold on tight, Takayama.

319
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:09,100
Yeah.

320
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,440
Take this!

321
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,500
Come on, give it back!

322
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:30,820
You little brat!

323
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:32,080
You went and got me too!

324
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,400
There it is!

325
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:49,620
How about that? Had enough?

326
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:51,660
Come on, give it back! The submarine!

327
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:52,080
Damn it!

328
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:01,500
My submarine!

329
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:01,920
Damn!

330
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:02,080
Dammit!

331
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,560
Kankichi-kun!

332
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:06,020
No way! Look at this!

333
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,060
Damn it, where is it?

334
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:12,160
Where? Where did it go?

335
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:17,975
It's my fault.

336
00:21:18,025 --> 00:21:21,700
If I'd just held back back there. Sorry.

337
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,077
No,

338
00:21:23,127 --> 00:21:26,560
It's not your fault, Kankichi-kun.
It's okay.

339
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:31,540
Wait right there.

340
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,560
K-Kankichi-kun

341
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:37,640
Kankichi

342
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,620
What now?

343
00:21:39,620 --> 00:21:41,260
This kid's soaking wet like that,

344
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,900
and now is not the time for that.

345
00:21:47,860 --> 00:21:50,260
Kifumiyo

346
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:52,960
It's nowhere near enough.

347
00:21:53,820 --> 00:21:54,480
Kinjirō

348
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,000
Hand over your piggy bank too.

349
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,240
Why would I? No way!

350
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,440
I'll pay you back even if I die!
Really! I swear on it!

351
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:13,640
Go!

352
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:17,500
Run!

353
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:35,920
Anpuchi!

354
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:40,540
What's wrong? The submarine contest is already over,
you know.

355
00:22:42,540 --> 00:22:44,740
Where's Takayama? Where is Takayama?

356
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:48,320
Takayama went home with his
little brother a while ago.

357
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,020
He looked really down, though.

358
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:55,140
He had no face to show us.

359
00:22:56,440 --> 00:23:00,620
But we should have taken the
model to Takayama's house back then.

360
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:06,200
Takayama-kun is suddenly moving
away because of his father's job.

361
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:10,460
Apparently he couldn't even say goodbye to everyone,
which is a real shame.

362
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,960
Showing up only now, of all times.

363
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:29,360
Senpai, are you really putting it back?

364
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:32,140
Returning it to its own
time is the best thing to do.

365
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:40,760
There are too many traces of memories here.

366
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:43,520
The places we played in as kids...

367
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:48,800
Alright, let's eat, eat.

368
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:51,100
Today I'm having tarasque!

369
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:51,620
Today?

370
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:53,180
Today too, right?

371
00:23:53,180 --> 00:23:53,640
Yeah.

372
00:24:14,740 --> 00:24:19,720
Packed train, a catnap on Dad's back

373
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:25,960
Another tough week,
and unreasonable demands are only natural

374
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:33,480
Though I act cool with one hand, it's a
beef bowl with extra soup, a little cloudy

375
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:40,360
Endless overtime frustration,
cleared away with more irritation

376
00:24:43,620 --> 00:24:50,140
Every day's no problem,
once I've gone through the hot shower

377
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:56,680
Every day's no problem,
energy restored with a sleep pillow

378
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:06,340
Every day's no problem,
I love a girl like me

379
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:09,440
Every day's no-brainer

380
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:13,160
Monday, with hearts flying everywhere

381
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:17,540
Andeck, andeck, no-brainer

382
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:22,180
What's with this golf course?

383
00:25:22,180 --> 00:25:24,060
It's right in the middle of town!

384
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:26,960
It was originally in the
middle of nature, though.

385
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:29,080
While we let nature take its course,

386
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,980
it just naturally turned out this way.

387
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:33,160
That's not natural at all!

388
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:37,300
Next time, the showdown: Great Nature Golf,
see you then!

